      "problem": "${(\\frac{1}{5})}^{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To raise the fraction to the power of $3$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $3:$\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{3}=\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{5}^{3}}\n$$\n\nNow, using ${1}^{3}=1$ and ${5}^{3}=125,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{5}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{125}.\n$$",
